<section class="section-line">
  <div class="narrow">
    <div class="eyebrow center">Where This Began</div>
    <h2 class="section-title center">David and the giant.</h2>
    <div class="meaning" style="margin-top:1.6rem">
      <p>Years before 490 Life, I built a little site called <em>David Slays Goliath</em>, a place to answer the giant-sized questions that keep people from God: What is the gospel? Can I trust the Bible? How do I even start reading it? What does a Christian life actually look like?</p>
      <p>I named it for the shepherd boy who walked at a giant with a sling and five smooth stones, because that story is the whole gospel in miniature: the battle is the Lord's, and He wins it through the unlikely. Those teachings are moving here, one by one. The giants haven't changed, and neither has the God who fells them.</p>
      <p>And the name on this site, 490, seventy times seven, is the answer Jesus gave when Peter asked how many times he had to forgive. Not a bigger number. The end of counting. I wrote <a href="/seventy-times-seven/">a whole book about it</a>, because I needed that answer as much as anyone I've ever preached it to.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

